---
kind: lore
id: isles.islands
title: The three islands
---

// AREA isles: the ferry calls (sail@isle.<island>), the three keepers and
// their beacons, the Mistral windmill puzzle and the Coralreach tide.

// ── the Isle Ferry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<beat id="sailFirstEmberkey" on="sail" target="isle.emberkey" title="Emberkey">
  ::bg{location="emberkey" time="day"}
  @narrator{code="0010"}: Emberkey is a black cone of rock with a village clinging to its skirt. Steam rises from cracks in the quay.
</beat>

<beat id="sailFirstMistral" on="sail" target="isle.mistral" title="Mistral Isle">
  ::bg{location="mistral" time="day"}
  @narrator{code="0010"}: Mistral Isle is all grass and wind. A windmill turns on the hill, its sails pointing the wrong way.
</beat>

<beat id="sailFirstCoralreach" on="sail" target="isle.coralreach" title="Coralreach">
  ::bg{location="coralreach" time="day"}
  @narrator{code="0010"}: Coralreach is barely an island at high tide: a lighthouse, three houses and a sea cave.
</beat>

<entry id="islesSailAgain" on="sail" target="kind:island" category="bark" priority="-10">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: The Isle Ferry noses in to {{occasion.target}}.
</entry>

// ── Keeper Brand, Emberkey ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

<beat use="beaconKeeper" id="brandRelight" isle="emberkey" keeper="emberkeyKeeper" thanks="My lens! Hand it here, hand it here. Up we go." instance="use-001"/>

<entry id="islesBrandBark" on="talk" target="npc.emberkeyKeeper" category="bark">
  @emberkeyKeeper{code="0010" when="!holds('islesRelit', ['emberkey'])"}: A grunt went up my tower with a sack and came down with my lens. He's still up there, if you can stand the heat.
  @emberkeyKeeper{code="0020" when="holds('islesRelit', ['emberkey'])"}: She burns like the old days. Look at her go.
</entry>

// ── Keeper Sorrel, Mistral Isle ─────────────────────────────────────────────

<beat use="beaconKeeper" id="sorrelRelight" isle="mistral" keeper="mistralKeeper" thanks="Oh, thank the wind. Give it here, carefully." instance="use-002">
  @mistralKeeper{code="0010" emotion="happy"}: The sails are right again, too. You have a knack.
</beat>

<entry id="islesSorrelBark" on="talk" target="npc.mistralKeeper" category="bark">
  @mistralKeeper{code="0010" when="run.islesVanes < 3"}: The grunt locked himself in the windmill loft. The hatch only opens when the sails face the wind, and he turned them all wrong.
  @mistralKeeper{code="0020" when="run.islesVanes >= 3"}: Sails are right. Now go and get my lens out of that loft.
</entry>

// The windmill: turn the three vanes into the wind. A wrong turn costs
// nothing; the puzzle stays until all three face the wind.
<beat id="windmill" on="enterPlace" target="place.mistralWindmill" title="The windmill" spentBy="run.islesVanes >= 3">
  ::bg{location="mistral-windmill" time="day"}
  @narrator{code="0010"}: Three wooden vanes, each on its own crank. The wind is coming off the sea, from the west. {{run.islesVanes:plural(One vane faces|# vanes face)}} it.
  <branch id="islesVane" prompt="Which way do you crank the next vane?">
    <choice id="west" label="Into the west wind">
      ::set{run.islesVanes += 1}
      @narrator{code="0020"}: The vane swings round and locks with a clunk.
    </choice>
    <choice id="east" label="Away from the wind">
      @narrator{code="0030"}: The vane spins, shudders, and swings back where it was.
    </choice>
  </branch>
</beat>

// ── Keeper Nerissa, Coralreach ──────────────────────────────────────────────

<beat use="beaconKeeper" id="nerissaRelight" isle="coralreach" keeper="coralreachKeeper" thanks="You went into the cave for it? At your age I'd have done the same. Come up." instance="use-003"/>

<entry id="islesNerissaBark" on="talk" target="npc.coralreachKeeper" category="bark">
  @coralreachKeeper{code="0010"}: The cave floods every afternoon. Go in the morning, when the tide is out.
</entry>

<entry id="islesCoralHighTide" on="enterPlace" target="place.coralCave" category="bark" priority="-10" when="!@islesLowTide">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: The sea cave's mouth is under water. The tide will be out in the morning.
</entry>
